n element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)={\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the diagram above, only the elements $-4$ and $0$ are mapped to $1.$ Therefore, the indicator function in the diagram above corresponds to the set $A={-4,0}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-21f37bd0-557b-529a-88f6-615287ca253d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-21f37bd0-557b-529a-88f6-615287ca253d" :answer-field/id #uuid "21f37bd0-557b-529a-88f6-615287ca253d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-357a177c-678c-5efe-b182-20eab09b9991" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d47d5aca-af9c-5149-840f-958902fb023e" "answer-1682b7b8-dbb8-5c5c-8816-d4c1a452d7d3" "answer-c0f9d3b8-8c93-55f3-9304-b50d10dc73ab" "answer-cc0455c7-2ede-5322-a0d7-f8002bc9bf9d" "answer-357a177c-678c-5efe-b182-20eab09b9991"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d47d5aca-af9c-5149-840f-958902fb023e" :answer/id #uuid "d47d5aca-af9c-5149-840f-958902fb023e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{-1,0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1682b7b8-dbb8-5c5c-8816-d4c1a452d7d3" :answer/id #uuid "1682b7b8-dbb8-5c5c-8816-d4c1a452d7d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{-3,-1,0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0f9d3b8-8c93-55f3-9304-b50d10dc73ab" :answer/id #uuid "c0f9d3b8-8c93-55f3-9304-b50d10dc73ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{-3,-2,-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc0455c7-2ede-5322-a0d7-f8002bc9bf9d" :answer/id #uuid "cc0455c7-2ede-5322-a0d7-f8002bc9bf9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{-4,-3,0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-357a177c-678c-5efe-b182-20eab09b9991" :answer/id #uuid "357a177c-678c-5efe-b182-20eab09b9991" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{-4,0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092600 :question/problem "![](images/b2/b2919328788c6762d1a0b56225b95749e88973ec84803584be0d336f63033566.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the subset $A$ of $U={a,b,c,d,e}$ whose indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ is shown above?" :question/worked-solution "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)={\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the diagram above, only the elements $a,b,$ and $d$ are mapped to $1.$ Therefore, the indicator function in the diagram above corresponds to the set $A={a,b,d}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d41cebf3-62a2-5784-a1f4-13fc481b665c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d41cebf3-62a2-5784-a1f4-13fc481b665c" :answer-field/id #uuid "d41cebf3-62a2-5784-a1f4-13fc481b665c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2fd26958-8f1d-57a3-abb9-807967b6f0e5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bb9403e9-592b-58af-9902-144607686e92" "answer-b32466f0-2c65-5408-a0aa-16fe5815df3d" "answer-2fd26958-8f1d-57a3-abb9-807967b6f0e5" "answer-31e4f699-7440-595b-9f7d-fd1e34e533f9" "answer-a5edb5b5-0109-53a0-8948-f6dbe9ed80b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb9403e9-592b-58af-9902-144607686e92" :answer/id #uuid "bb9403e9-592b-58af-9902-144607686e92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a,b,c,d}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b32466f0-2c65-5408-a0aa-16fe5815df3d" :answer/id #uuid "b32466f0-2c65-5408-a0aa-16fe5815df3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a,b,c}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fd26958-8f1d-57a3-abb9-807967b6f0e5" :answer/id #uuid "2fd26958-8f1d-57a3-abb9-807967b6f0e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a,b,d}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31e4f699-7440-595b-9f7d-fd1e34e533f9" :answer/id #uuid "31e4f699-7440-595b-9f7d-fd1e34e533f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{c,e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5edb5b5-0109-53a0-8948-f6dbe9ed80b9" :answer/id #uuid "a5edb5b5-0109-53a0-8948-f6dbe9ed80b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{d,e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092602 :question/problem "$$\n{1}_{A}(5)=1,\\,{1}_{B}(5)=0\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(5)=1$\n- ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(5)=0$\n- $5\\in A\\cap B$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(5) & =min{{1}_{A}(5),{1}_{B}(5)} \\\\  & =min{1,0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(5)=0,$ we conclude that $5$ does not belong to $A\\cap B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5dc6e1da-5a6c-5d24-ae2f-76a4c9c09715"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5dc6e1da-5a6c-5d24-ae2f-76a4c9c09715" :answer-field/id #uuid "5dc6e1da-5a6c-5d24-ae2f-76a4c9c09715" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1737c9b3-9afe-57ff-999b-4fa97a61723d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-95407129-ac58-5f82-82c8-97ce4f4156cd" "answer-f0066faa-d1eb-5427-ab3c-9e44126bd655" "answer-1737c9b3-9afe-57ff-999b-4fa97a61723d" "answer-844ca5b4-a0c6-5ba0-9623-57c490152861" "answer-49cb469a-be52-5791-8807-8b802f15d5ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95407129-ac58-5f82-82c8-97ce4f4156cd" :answer/id #uuid "95407129-ac58-5f82-82c8-97ce4f4156cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0066faa-d1eb-5427-ab3c-9e44126bd655" :answer/id #uuid "f0066faa-d1eb-5427-ab3c-9e44126bd655" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1737c9b3-9afe-57ff-999b-4fa97a61723d" :answer/id #uuid "1737c9b3-9afe-57ff-999b-4fa97a61723d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-844ca5b4-a0c6-5ba0-9623-57c490152861" :answer/id #uuid "844ca5b4-a0c6-5ba0-9623-57c490152861" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49cb469a-be52-5791-8807-8b802f15d5ed" :answer/id #uuid "49cb469a-be52-5791-8807-8b802f15d5ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-92b8a61e-f7a9-5e1e-adba-90e2fa6c6243" :question/id #uuid "92b8a61e-f7a9-5e1e-adba-90e2fa6c6243" :question/math-academy-id "q-174394" :question/problem "$$\n{1}_{A}(-1)=1,\\,{1}_{B}(-1)=1\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=1$\n- ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=0$\n- $-1\\in A\\cap B$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1) & =min{{1}_{A}(-1),{1}_{B}(-1)} \\\\  & =min{1,1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=1,$ we conclude that $-1$ belongs to $A\\cap B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-652fe437-abe7-5a5a-bb3a-38f7c9e05f8f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-652fe437-abe7-5a5a-bb3a-38f7c9e05f8f" :answer-field/id #uuid "652fe437-abe7-5a5a-bb3a-38f7c9e05f8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7bdeb40f-7a93-51cd-bc84-fa02eb15dc72" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7bdeb40f-7a93-51cd-bc84-fa02eb15dc72" "answer-f75b591c-4385-5f6c-a77e-5445cd4d5bf5" "answer-1a0cc322-449d-5a1c-a8d7-1039e1ba0529" "answer-9366fcca-3b9b-567c-9045-3a0693b79cf8" "answer-de642bb2-a99e-53bd-8f67-e1c68961beb6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bdeb40f-7a93-51cd-bc84-fa02eb15dc72" :answer/id #uuid "7bdeb40f-7a93-51cd-bc84-fa02eb15dc72" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f75b591c-4385-5f6c-a77e-5445cd4d5bf5" :answer/id #uuid "f75b591c-4385-5f6c-a77e-5445cd4d5bf5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a0cc322-449d-5a1c-a8d7-1039e1ba0529" :answer/id #uuid "1a0cc322-449d-5a1c-a8d7-1039e1ba0529" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9366fcca-3b9b-567c-904